[ti:Day 19]

[00:00.00]ambition [æmˈbɪʃn]n. 野心；雄心，抱负；追求的目标 vt. 追求；有…野心 例 With all their passion and ambition, they should have an intuitive understanding of cycles and markets.
[00:15.84]board [bɔːd]n. (企业、学校等的)董事会，理事会；委 员会；部门 例 As the chairman of the board, he has supreme power. 搭 across the board 包括一切地；全面地 / take on board 考虑
[00:29.88]manageress [ˌmænɪdʒəˈres]n. 女经理；女财务管理人
[00:34.20]astute [əˈstjuːt]a. 敏锐的，精明的；狡猾的 例 Astute businesses keep pace with changes by paying attention to such factors as personnel changes, new product lines, etc.
[00:50.28]classify [ˈklæsɪfaɪ]vt. 分类，归类 例 As we classify these users by project, the defect database appears to be unique for each user and each project.
[01:04.68]abeyance [əˈbeɪəns]n. 中止，搁置；(所有权等的) 未定 例 The law will be left in abeyance once the state's security is threatened. 搭 in abeyance 暂停使用，搁置
[01:18.48]warring [ˈwɔːrɪŋ]a. 交战的；敌对的；冲突的 n. 战斗；敌 对行动 搭 warring sides 敌对双方
[01:25.08]ethical [ˈeθɪkl]a. 道德的，伦理的；合乎职业道德标准的 例 Some new drugs do face the ethical dilemma.
[01:33.60]etiquette [ˈetɪkət]n. 礼节；礼仪；规矩，成规 例 It's proper table etiquette to leave an appropriate tip after the meal.
[01:44.64]tenet [ˈtenɪt]n. 原则；信条，宗旨 例 We will make technology innovation our central tenet of development.
[01:54.60]outset [ˈaʊtset]n. 开始，开端 搭 at/from the outset (从一)开始，起初
[02:00.36]rebuff [rɪˈbʌf]vt. 断然拒绝；挫败 n. 断然拒绝 搭 rebuff an invitation from sb. 回绝某人的邀请 / suffer a rebuff from sb. 遭到某人的拒绝
[02:11.28]showcase [ˈʃəʊkeɪs]n. 陈列橱；显示优点的东西 vt. 展览； 使显出优点 例 The project can fully showcase your leadership skills.
[02:22.08]uncollectible [ˌʌnkəˈlektəbl]a. 无法收集的；不可收回的；无法 收款的
[02:27.72]accordance [əˈkɔːdns]n. 一致；和谐；给予 例 In accordance with the law, women enjoy equal rights with men in their political and economic life. 搭 in accordance with 与…一致；按照，依据 floor price 底价，最低限价
[02:46.68]exterior [ɪkˈstɪəriə(r)]n. 外面；外表 a. 外面的；外来的； 对外的 例 Our offlce building has an exterior stairway.
[02:56.64]propagate [ˈprɒpəɡeɪt]vt. 传播；传送；使普及，宣传 搭 propagate scientific knowledge 普及科学知 识
[03:05.16]campaign [kæmˈpeɪn]n. 运动；游说；(商业、竞选) 活动 vi. 参加运动；开展运动 例 The company is going to break the sales campaign with a parade in May. 搭 campaign against 开展运动以反对 / campaign for 开展运动以支持
[03:22.80]straightforward [ˌstreɪtˈfɔːwəd]a. 简单的；坦率的；直接的 ad. 直截了当地；坦率地 搭 straightforward dialogue 直截了当的对话 / straightforward reply 坦率的回答
[03:36.36]pending [ˈpendɪŋ]prep. 直到…时为止；在…期间 a. 待决 的，未决的；即将发生的
[03:42.00]drawback [ˈdrɔːbæk]n. 缺点；不利条件 例 Slow speed is the chief drawback of sea shipment.
[03:50.28]arrears [əˈrɪəz]n. 应付欠款，逾期债款；待完成的事 例 Due to the immature development of construction market and imperfect credit system, the arrears of wages is a very big problem. 搭 in arrears 拖欠
[04:08.52]margin [ˈmɑːdʒɪn]n. (成本与售价间的)差额；利润，毛 利；保证金；差数；幅度；边缘 例 This year our company plans to decrease the investment in project development by a wide margin.
[04:24.00]induce [ɪnˈdjuːs]vt. 引起；导致；引诱 例 What induced you to leave the company? 搭 induce sb. to do sth. 劝诱某人做某事
[04:34.20]quintessence [kwɪnˈtesns]n. 精华，精髓；典型，典范 例 Peking Opera is believed to be the quintessence of Chinese culture.
[04:45.60]accommodate [əˈkɒmədeɪt]vt. 为…提供食宿；为…提供方便(或 服务)；接纳；使适应；调和 例 The bank accommodated him with a loan of 5 million dollars. 搭 accommodate sb. with sth. 向某人提供某物
[05:01.68]bonus [ˈbəʊnəs]n. 奖金，额外津贴；红利，额外股息
[05:05.40]laden [ˈleɪdn]a. 装载的；装满的；苦恼的 例 The laden ship called at New York Harbor. 搭 be laden with 满载 / laden draught 满载吃水
[05:16.44]abode [əˈbəʊd]n. 住所，寄居；营业所；停留 例 The creative use of recycled materials also features in sustainable designs for both humble and high-end abodes. 搭 make one's abode 居住 / take up one's abode with sb. 开始与某人同住
[05:37.08]curb [kɜːb]vt. 勒住；控制 n. 勒马索；控制 a. 场外(证 券)交易的 例 We do need to act convincingly to curb future deflcits. 搭 put a curb on 对…进行控制
[05:49.20]variable [ˈveəriəbl]n. 可变因素；变量 a. 易变的；可变 的，可调节的
[05:54.24]verify [ˈverɪfaɪ]vt. 核实；查证，证实；检验
[05:57.84]velocity [vəˈlɒsəti]n. 速率；速度；周转率
[06:01.44]repeal [rɪˈpiːl]vt. 废止；撤销；放弃；否定 n. 废除；撤 销；作废 例 The immigration act was repealed flnally.
[06:10.56]increment [ˈɪŋkrəmənt]n. 增额；增值；盈余
[06:14.28]convention [kənˈvenʃn]n. (国际性)公约，协定；规范；惯 例 ； ； 搭 break down old conventions 打破常规
[06:22.56]upgrade [ˌʌpˈɡreɪd]n. 升级；上升 vt. 使升级；提高价格； 改进，改善 例 There is room for the amusement park to upgrade its tickets. 搭 on the upgrade 上升的；欣欣向荣的
[06:36.36]antecedent [ˌæntɪˈsiːdnt]n. 先辈；前事；履历，经历 a. 先前 的 例 The training focuses on the antecedent, or the environment and events that set the stage for a tantrum or other undesirable action.
[06:54.72]freight [freɪt]n. (运输中的)货物；货运；运费 vt. 运送(货 物)；装货于 (船等) 例 Please quote us prices including insurance and freight to Vancouver. 搭 by freight 用普通铁路货车运送(区别于by express，用快车运送)
[07:12.24]kermis [ˈkɜːmɪs]n. 露天集市；慈善义卖市场 例 Selling secondhand books at the kermis, I got into an argument with a customer.
[07:23.64]jargon [ˈdʒɑːɡən]n. 行话；专用术语 vi. 说行话 例 She has been used to skipping the jargon and getting some ideas when reading the economics magazines. 搭 technical jargon 技术术语；专业术语
[07:40.68]complain [kəmˈpleɪn]v. 抱怨；申诉，控诉 例 You complain he treats you like other employees, but what is he supposed to do? 搭 complain about 抱怨 / complain to sb. of sth. 向某人控诉某事
[07:57.24]gamble [ˈɡæmbl]n. 冒险，投机；赌博 v. 冒险；赌博 例 His gamble turned out to be a stroke of business genius. 搭 gamble away 赌光 / gamble on (doing) sth. 以(做)…打赌
[08:11.40]glide [ɡlaɪd]vi. 滑动，滑行；(时间等)消逝；(事情)渐 变 n. 滑动，滑行 例 Waiters glide among tightly-packed tables bearing trays of pasta. 搭 glide landing 下滑着陆 / glide path 滑行道
[08:27.00]voyage [ˈvɔɪɪdʒ]n. 航程；航空；航海；航行时间 vi. 航 海，航行 vt. 渡过，飞过 搭 make a voyage to... 航行到…
[08:35.04]moratorium [ˌmɒrəˈtɔːriəm]n. 延期偿付(权)；延期偿付期 间；暂停，中止
[08:40.68]dodge [dɒdʒ]vi. 躲避；逃避责任 vt. 躲避 n. 推托，搪 塞 例 Some will tackle questions head on, while others will dodge them entirely. 搭 on the dodge 无固定住处以逃避追捕
[08:54.84]allowance [əˈlaʊəns]n. 津贴，补助；限额，定量 例 Employees in the company can get an monthly allowance of 100 dollars for trafflc expenditure.
