[09:50.76]solicitor [səˈlɪsɪtə(r)]n. 初级律师，事务律师；掮客；游说 者
[09:55.68]line [laɪn]n. 路线，航线；行业；系列产品；经营范 围；界限 v. 排成一行 例 The new plan is to complete the reformation of the old product line. 搭 in line with 符合；与…一致 / out of line 不 协调，不一致
[10:11.40]materiality [məˌtɪərɪˈælətɪ]n. 重要性；物质性 例 He emphasised the materiality of the compensation allocation flrst.
[10:22.92]autonomy [ɔːˈtɒnəmi]n. 自治，自治权；自主，自主权；独 立 例 Branch managers will have full autonomy in their own areas. 搭 autonomy in decision-making 作决定的自主 权
[10:37.44]audacious [ɔːˈdeɪʃəs]a. 大胆创新的，有冒险精神的；鲁莽 冒失的，厚颜无耻的 例 Given all that, how could such an audacious project get the go-ahead? 搭 audacious attempt 大胆的尝试
[10:52.68]leakage [ˈliːkɪdʒ]n. 漏，泄漏；漏损；漏出量 例 The drastic blast did not result in radiation leakage.
[11:01.92]pump [pʌmp]n. 泵；抽水机 vt. 用泵抽(水)；盘问；激 励 例 A pump is listed in spare parts order number 318.
[11:10.68]breakeven [ˈbreɪkiːvn]a. 无亏损的 n. 收支平衡 例 The company said its operating margin for devices and services could be around breakeven.
