[12:35.16]speculate [ˈspekjuleɪt]vi. 推测；做投机买卖
[12:39.12]stark [stɑːk]a. 严格的，刻板的；完全的，全然的 ad. 完全；明显地 搭 stark denial 完全否认 / stark discipline 严格 的纪律 rat race 〈俚〉(商界)日常紧张的竞争；无意义的竞争 例 I have got tired of the rat race and determined to resign. 我已经厌倦了这种毫无意 义的竞争，决定辞职不干了。
[13:00.12]warrant [ˈwɒrənt]n. 授权；收款凭证；许可证 vt. 保证， 担保；批准
[13:04.92]log [lɒɡ]n. 测程仪；航海日志；记录 vt. 把…记入航 行日志；登录 例 Common users are not allowed to log onto the enterprise intranet. 搭 performance log 运行情况记录 / sail by the log 靠测程仪测船位
[13:20.76]sterile [ˈsteraɪl]a. 贫瘠的；不能升值的；无效果的；无 结果的；无菌的，消过毒的 搭 sterile cabinet 无菌操作柜
[13:28.80]vagary [ˈveɪɡəri]n. [pl.] 奇想；异想天开；异常行为；难 以预测的情况 例 The issue is considered as a major vagary of doing business in Western countries.
[13:42.24]crumble [ˈkrʌmbl]vi. 破碎；崩溃 例 Thanks to these companies the old restrictions have started to crumble. 搭 crumble to dust 垮掉，化为乌有
[13:55.08]impose [ɪmˈpəʊz]vt. 把…强加于；征(税等)；处以(罚 款、监禁等) vi. 利用；打扰；欺骗 例 You should state the charges rather than impose them upon others. 搭 impose...on 把…强加于 / impose on 利用； 欺骗
[14:11.64]flatter [ˈflætə(r)]vt. 向…奉承，阿谀；使高兴，使满意 例 It is said that a sure way to flatter Caesar is to remind him how he hates flatterers. 搭 flatter oneself 自豪；自以为是
[14:27.00]heyday [ˈheɪdeɪ]n. 全盛时期，兴旺期 例 During the postal system's heyday, unmanned electric trains lugged daily loads of 4 million letters. 搭 reach the heyday 到达全盛期
